// Armor and splash (WP5.3, docs/rules/armour.md), on a 64 by 64 cell open map (no terrain layer). A hit takes
// the percentage of the armor table (damage type against the victim's armor type) and a weapon with a
// splash radius also hurts what is near where it goes off. What the run shows, one group at a time; all the
// shooters are owner 0, the targets owner 1 unless it says otherwise:
//   A  Bullets     a rifleman on a heavy tank (10 percent of 6 is 3/5: one hit point a shot), one on a light
//                  tank (40 percent: 2) and one on a rifleman (100 percent: 6; the 9th shot kills).
//   B  Rockets     a rocket thrower on a light tank (130 percent of 45 is 58.5: 59), on a heavy tank (100:
//                  45) and on a rifleman (40: 18, three rockets).
//   C  Sniper      the long rifle does 0 percent to a heavy tank (the shots are fired, nothing comes off)
//                  and 40 to a rocket thrower (45 hit points: the second shot kills).
//   E  Howitzer    one shell on a rifleman in the middle of a crowd. The splash is 1.5 cells with full
//                  strength out to 0.5 from the edge of a body: a rifleman a cell away takes 63, a light
//                  tank next to the target 68 (75 percent of 90, a tie rounded up), a heavy tank two cells
//                  off 11 (50 percent of 90 at a quarter), a generator next to it 135 (150 percent); a
//                  rocket thrower two cells off is outside; a rifleman of the SHOOTER'S side next to the
//                  target dies with it (friendly fire).
//   F  Bombs       a bomb of 60 with a splash of 2 (full out to 1) on a heavy tank: 30 (50 percent) direct,
//                  and the bystanders: a friendly rifleman a cell off takes the full 60 (it dies) from `bomb`
//                  and nothing from `careful_bomb`; an enemy rifleman two cells off takes 12 either way.
//   G  Self        a bomb team that bombs an enemy next to it is in its own blast and goes down with the
//                  target; the careful one is not.
// CI runs it on Linux and Windows and requires the checksum in armour_splash.expected;
// tools/sf_headless/tests/armour_splash.rs asserts the numbers above along the way.
//
// `unit_defs` names a FROZEN copy of the definitions (armour_splash_defs/): a balance change of
// assets/config/ does not move this checksum. The copy is the shipped set of WP5.3 with two additions:
// the weapons `bomb` and `careful_bomb` and the units `bomb_team` (90) and `careful_bomb_team` (91) that
// carry them. The reload of the bombs is longer than the run: each team drops exactly one. `combat: true`
// gives the world the weapon table, with the armor table.
// Owners: 0 Meridian, 1 Veyran. Everything stands on the middle of its cell.
//
// Entity ids, all at generation 0, in the order the spawns are written:
//    0  rifleman RA1 (12)                owner 0  cell (4, 4)    A: attacks 1
//    1  heavy_tank TA1 (20, 900 hp)      owner 1  cell (8, 4)
//    2  rifleman RA2                     owner 0  cell (4, 8)    A: attacks 3
//    3  rifleman VA2 (50 hp)             owner 1  cell (8, 8)
//    4  rifleman RA3                     owner 0  cell (4, 12)   A: attacks 5
//    5  light_tank TA3 (19, 400 hp)      owner 1  cell (8, 12)
//    6  rocket_trooper RB1 (13)          owner 0  cell (14, 4)   B: attacks 7
//    7  light_tank TB1                   owner 1  cell (18, 4)
//    8  rocket_trooper RB2               owner 0  cell (14, 8)   B: attacks 9
//    9  heavy_tank TB2                   owner 1  cell (18, 8)
//   10  rocket_trooper RB3               owner 0  cell (14, 12)  B: attacks 11
//   11  rifleman VB3                     owner 1  cell (18, 12)
//   12  sniper SC1 (16, long rifle)      owner 0  cell (24, 4)   C: attacks 13
//   13  heavy_tank TC1                   owner 1  cell (30, 4)
//   14  sniper SC2                       owner 0  cell (24, 8)   C: attacks 15
//   15  rocket_trooper VC2 (45 hp)       owner 1  cell (30, 8)
//   16  siege_artillery AE (21)          owner 0  cell (6, 30)   E: attacks 17
//   17  rifleman TE                      owner 1  cell (6, 22)   E: the middle of the burst
//   18  rifleman E1                      owner 1  cell (7, 22)   E: a cell east
//   19  heavy_tank E2                    owner 1  cell (6, 24)   E: two cells south
//   20  light_tank E3                    owner 1  cell (5, 22)   E: a cell west
//   21  generator E4 (40, a structure)   owner 1  cell (6, 21)   E: a cell north
//   22  rocket_trooper E5                owner 1  cell (6, 20)   E: two cells north
//   23  rifleman E6                      owner 0  cell (6, 23)   E: a cell south, the shooter's own side
//   24  bomb_team BF1 (90)               owner 0  cell (24, 22)  F: attacks 25
//   25  heavy_tank TF1                   owner 1  cell (30, 22)
//   26  rifleman FF1                     owner 0  cell (31, 22)  F: a friend, a cell east of the target
//   27  rifleman FE1                     owner 1  cell (30, 24)  F: an enemy, two cells south
//   28  careful_bomb_team BF2 (91)       owner 0  cell (24, 28)  F: attacks 29
//   29  heavy_tank TF2                   owner 1  cell (30, 28)
//   30  rifleman FF2                     owner 0  cell (31, 28)  F: a friend
//   31  rifleman FE2                     owner 1  cell (30, 30)  F: an enemy
//   32  bomb_team BG1                    owner 0  cell (20, 36)  G: attacks 33
//   33  rifleman VG1                     owner 1  cell (21, 36)
//   34  careful_bomb_team BG2            owner 0  cell (28, 36)  G: attacks 35
//   35  rifleman VG2                     owner 1  cell (29, 36)
